    "m2_prompt_trader_proposal_original": "**Action**: Hold\n\n**Reasoning**: The investment plan calls for a Hold on AMZN, and the evidence supports this balanced stance. The long-term structural case remains intact \u2014 AMZN trades 15.8% above a rising 200-day SMA, Q1 2024 operating cash flow of $18.99B is the strongest Q1 in company history, and the equity base is solid at 40.8% equity-to-assets. However, short-term technicals have deteriorated: price is below the 10-day EMA ($183.27) and 50-day SMA ($181.92), MACD histogram is negative and expanding (-0.80), RSI is falling at 44.48, and the 5-day return is -2.14%. Fundamental data is incomplete (no revenue, net income, EPS, or margins available), and net cash after reinvestment is essentially zero (-$0.13B), providing no margin of safety. The bull wins on the long-term structural case; the bear wins on near-term tactical momentum. This is the definition of a Hold \u2014 maintain existing positions, do not add into a falling knife, and wait for confirmation signals (reclaim of $183.27 with volume, or a bullish reversal at the $176.97-$175 support zone) before adding exposure.\n\n**Stop Loss**: 175.0\n\n**Position Sizing**: Maintain existing positions at neutral weight; do not add new exposure until confirmation signals appear. If adding on confirmation, scale in gradually in one-third tranches.\n\nFINAL TRANSACTION PROPOSAL: **HOLD**",
